---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Heirloom Support: Help With the Old Letter Reader App"
      description="Help with Heirloom: Old Letter Reader. Scanning tips, fixing transcriptions, offline use, subscriptions and how to contact support."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main">
      <h1>Heirloom Support</h1>
      <p>
        Need help with scanning, transcription, subscriptions, or a technical issue?
        Contact us and include your device model, iOS version, and a description of what happened.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:randyventures06@gmail.com">randyventures06@gmail.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>How many pages can I scan at once?</h3>
      <p>
        Scan or import up to five pages for a letter, then check and reorder them before Heirloom
        reads them. Each saved letter keeps its original pages so you can zoom in and compare them
        with the text.
      </p>
      <h3>The transcription has a mistake. Can I fix it?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. You can correct the transcript, the modernized text, or the translation on your device
        without another AI request. The original AI text is kept, and Heirloom reminds you to check
        the related versions after a correction. AI can misread handwriting or leave text out, so
        always check names, dates and unclear passages against the original page.
      </p>
      <h3>How do I get a better result?</h3>
      <p>
        Photograph the page flat in soft daylight without flash, hold the phone parallel to the
        page, and keep the whole page in the frame. Results depend on the writing and the photo
        quality. For more tips, read
        <a href="/blog/how-to-read-old-cursive-letters/">how to read old cursive letters</a>.
      </p>
      <h3>Does Heirloom need an internet connection?</h3>
      <p>
        Reading a letter with AI needs a connection, and the selected photos are sent to the reading
        service for processing. Saved letters and your edits are stored on your device.
      </p>
      <h3>How do subscriptions work?</h3>
      <p>
        Your first page is free and fully unlocked. Heirloom Unlimited offers weekly or yearly
        auto-renewing subscriptions for continued reading, with prices shown before purchase. Manage
        or cancel a subscription in your Apple account settings. To restore a purchase on a new
        device, sign in with the same Apple account.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Read the <a href={'/heirloom/privacy/'}>Heirloom Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>